{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society","id":1258338,"title":"What if The Fae rules a Unified Supernatural Society?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-30T23:39:24-07:00","id":1258338,"title":"What if The Fae rules a Unified Supernatural Society?","content":"What if the Fae capitalized on their superior numbers and godlike potential and became the ruling class of supernatural in most of the world? Like what if like in the Middle Kingdom the Supernaturals are at least cordial with each other?<br /> <br /> So in this setting say either the Fae couldn\u2019t escape to Arcadia because it collapsed, or maybe the Fomorians warred with the Tuatha stirred by the Black Plague?<br /> <br /> So the Fae instead of having their Faeholds dragged off the World just took root. They adapted on mass either becoming Changelings or Anchored Inanimae. Say the Fae decided to take a hand on the reigns of the supernatural world. They involved themselves in the Anarch revolt, volunteering an ultimatum, accept shelter amid their Courts or be driven from their Lairs into the fires of the Inquisition. Making a point of shattering even the Eldest rather then diablerise it, and Driving Lasombra itself into the Abyss. Cainites now operate under the court of the Fae. The Salubri were accepted and the Tremere crushed in their infancy, now only existing as a small bloodline guarded by Gargoyles and Demons. Vampire embraces are regulated now by local lords.<br /> <br /> The Traditions and the Order of Reason war was decided when the traditions accepted position as wisemen and seers for the Fae to tend the sacred places of the world. They broke the Order of Reason. They now exist as a conspiracy across the World, seeking to guide the light of Reason in secret.<br /> <br /> Some of the Early shelters from the Echos of Faith and Banality came in the form of the Fae bringing some of their holdings into the lands of the Dead, not completely dominating the dead but establishing themselves as the Hades and Zeranbooches of the Dead. When given the choice of being soul forged in the atheist war forges of the Dark Kingdoms or finding Dust or Paradise among the Old Gods the Dark Kingdoms are not as they would be if they were undisputed.<br /> <br /> The Fera find War and Peace with the Fae, ultimately they take up their ages old position as the Wardens of Doomsday and they gain perhaps better relations with some Courts over others.<br /> <br /> By modern days Vampires are much less populous then the default setting, perhaps no more then a fourth their number, and many take more supernatural airs, like the Laibon, becoming more prone to demonic or beastial features if they embrace monstrousness.<br /> <br /> Most supernaturals consider themselves as part of the World of Darkness, their name for the hidden supernatural facet of reality. Mostly ruled by Fae Nobles, or Elders, there are some Vampires and Mages who hold positions of power, but rarely officially leaders of anything but their own kind, more commonly generals or Seers of Dukes and Sultans of the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T16:18:38-07:00","id":1258440,"title":"","content":"Fae are powerful but there are plenty of Gods to go around. Kindred don't want to be servants of Faries. Mages sure as hell don't. While there will always be traitors I Imagine instead of the one world success you get the Fairy host becomes a bit like the Camarila. They are the standard and impose a certain type of order on the SUpernatural.. but there's plenty of Sabbat equivalents, plenty of various supernaturals who do not buy into their game and can drive them out of domains.<br /> <br /> If the Salubri sell out kindred kind, I'd imagine the Tremere gain yet another point of &quot;WE WERE RIGHT&quot; between their magics and the support of the High clans I can imagine the Tremere form a block including the Lasombra and the Ventrue. While they might fight amongst eachother even worse would be be the audacity of letting something else win! The Brujah and Capadocians(who get to surive here) would I imagine follow suit for similar reasons.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu side with the faries and much of them are converted into Gargoyles for their troubles.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel attempt to maintain neutrality and are only smashed for their troubles eventually having versions of the clan on each side of the divide.<br /> <br /> The Tzim are destroyed, they would not bend and they would not unite, struck by bothsides they at best live on as flesh crafters under fairy dominion.. or as Gargoyles.<br /> <br /> The Toreador are the first and formost to take the Fairy offer, they are the Eunich princes, the pampered pets of Fairy kind. <br /> <br /> The Malkavians take a similar situation.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos are potentially the most dangerous factor to the Fairies and ultimately are forced to join up with the Nascent Kindred rebellion.<br /> <br /> The Assamites probably weather the storm.<br /> <br /> The Settites try to play both sides while maintaining some sense of independence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Werewolf- the Fianna fall. They fall hard and become the servants of the of the Fae while I imagine the Garou nation adds a whole bunch of &quot;Fight the Fae/wyld&quot; to its litany.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mage- You've just completely undercut any justification for the Traditions. The Order of Reason is in all ways right in this timeline. The Traditions never form. The Order of Reason is a bit more open to other &quot;Reasonable&quot; groups pulling in the Remains of the ORder of Hermes and the would be Solfacti, It may even include the Ali-batin and the Wu Lung(if they see the threat). The Defenders of Humanity against the supernatural. There will be many disparate groups, and those who serve the Fae will be seen as not too different from NEphandi, they have rejected the call of Ascension for another Road.<br /> <br /> Wraith-Going into the deadlands is probably not a good idea at the end of the day, the touch of Oblivion cannot be all that helpful.. and there's alot of ghosts... Ghost numbers probably beat all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> OVerall though I'd imagine the biggest change would be on mortal society, The horrible things in the woods have conquered the world and driven out the strongest of faiths... Except at the edges of the map where the Order of Reason has well imposed Reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T02:19:12-07:00","id":1258514,"title":"","content":"Well no, I\u2019m not saying the conquered the mortal world, that\u2019s for the time of judgement when the Tuatha and Fomorians return. I\u2019m saying they are just the big cheese in the shadows. So yeah like a broad camarilla type concept for all supernaturals, like the shen of the Middle Kingdom, but the Fae just being most prominent.<br /> <br /> So I don\u2019t see the Traditions falling apart, they are just aligned with the Fae to keep magic in the world, tough I can see more of them becoming morally grey, dipping into hedonism, occult secrets, or bloody sacrifices to save the Magic of the world. They won the Paradigm war.<br /> <br /> And yes Ghosts outnumber even the Fae probably a thousand to one. But a few things. First an individual ghost is rarely more potent then a mortal, most barely know more then the beginnings of an arcanoi or two. And two wraiths fight everyone including each other. So they could arguably be even less unified the default, with many of them siding with the gods of Death that many Fae appear to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> Only the release of Demons from the Abyss could challenge the Faes Number and easy potence... and I say they would be greeted as a type of Gallain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T20:27:34-07:00","id":1258661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1258514#post1258514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well no, I\u2019m not saying the conquered the mortal world, that\u2019s for the time of judgement when the Tuatha and Fomorians return. I\u2019m saying they are just the big cheese in the shadows. So yeah like a broad camarilla type concept for all supernaturals, like the shen of the Middle Kingdom, but the Fae just being most prominent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see even if the fae don't rule openly a world where the Fae have taken over supernatural society leading to an earth like the Modern WOD. Especially if they are promoting &quot;More magic&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I don\u2019t see the Traditions falling apart, they are just aligned with the Fae to keep magic in the world, tough I can see more of them becoming morally grey, dipping into hedonism, occult secrets, or bloody sacrifices to save the Magic of the world. They won the Paradigm war. </div> </div> </div>The Traditions don't come together. THe shattering happens before the Council of Nine forms. While I can see quite a few groups selling out to be &quot;Faephandus&quot; to serve the fae is to reject ascension. You don't have any form of the Celestial Chorus, You don't have the Order of Hermes, You don't have the Akashic Brotherhood, You don't have the Euthanatos. You Don't have the Ali batini. You potentially have bits that could be the Verbena, the Ecstatics and some of the Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> In the face of the Order of Reason being completely right I'd see the Hermetics Chorus and the Solfacti siding with the Order rather than paradigm warring. The Fae are the threat. Mankind's destiny really is being taken by the monsters(more so than in the standard WOD)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes Ghosts outnumber even the Fae probably a thousand to one. But a few things. First an individual ghost is rarely more potent then a mortal, most barely know more then the beginnings of an arcanoi or two. And two wraiths fight everyone including each other. So they could arguably be even less unified the default, with many of them siding with the gods of Death that many Fae appear to be. </div> </div> </div>If you've been raised to Worship jesus and then suddenly Hades shows up and you've generally been told &quot;Hades was just a mask for demons&quot; all your life are you going to start worshipping him? Because that's going to be the case in Europe. And no the Empire of Stygia is perhaps in one of its more united, and mortals.. ARE a danger to fae at the time so a whole bunch of Ghosts are probably capable at the very least of keeping the Fae from conquering the Dark Kingdoms. The Fae probably have theirown little areas though<br /> <br /> Potentially if all the groups united they could throw off the Fae.. but they won't. They are as much enemies of eachother. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T22:52:18-07:00","id":1258673,"title":"","content":"**<br /> I don't see even if the fae don't rule openly a world where the Fae have taken over supernatural society leading to an earth like the Modern WOD. Especially if they are promoting &quot;More magic&quot;<br /> **<br /> For the same reason they don\u2019t in the normal world. They get in each others way. But perhaps it is a bit better in some ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> **<br /> The Traditions don't come together. THe shattering happens before the Council of Nine forms. While I can see quite a few groups selling out to be &quot;Faephandus&quot; to serve the fae is to reject ascension. You don't have any form of the Celestial Chorus, You don't have the Order of Hermes, You don't have the Akashic Brotherhood, You don't have the Euthanatos. You Don't have the Ali batini. You potentially have bits that could be the Verbena, the Ecstatics and some of the Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> In the face of the Order of Reason being completely right I'd see the Hermetics Chorus and the Solfacti siding with the Order rather than paradigm warring. The Fae are the threat. Mankind's destiny really is being taken by the monsters(more so than in the standard WOD)<br /> **<br /> This is incorrect, the Dark Age Gameline is after the Sundering but before the Shattering. Hermetics Exist. The Messiac precursors of the Choristers Exist, same with most of the others including the Batini and the Euthanatoi. The First Cabal already existed.<br /> <br /> <br /> **<br /> If you've been raised to Worship jesus and then suddenly Hades shows up and you've generally been told &quot;Hades was just a mask for demons&quot; all your life are you going to start worshipping him? Because that's going to be the case in Europe. And no the Empire of Stygia is perhaps in one of its more united, and mortals.. ARE a danger to fae at the time so a whole bunch of Ghosts are probably capable at the very least of keeping the Fae from conquering the Dark Kingdoms. The Fae probably have theirown little areas though<br /> <br /> Potentially if all the groups united they could throw off the Fae.. but they won't. They are as much enemies of eachother. <br /> **<br /> Thats not quite accurate. If it was the Fishers or some other religious order would be ruling the Dead, for a time they got close but nope the dead are more pragmatic and often lacking in Faith of unseen angels when Satyrs are right there. But in my canon Angels and Demons exist as Gallain. But huge thing, if you work for Stygia all mass has to come from Plundered Relics and literally making objects out of souls... Fae and Mages can create plasmic matter from their miracle powers. They can literally create Heaven and without literally needing to make the spiked pits or food out of Wraiths. They can literally create the food of paradise from their godlike powers... that absolutely is not something to ignore. And the oldest and most potent of the Dead worship the Old Ways. But either way I view everything from Angels to Egyptian Demons existing among the Fae in some form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T10:39:54-07:00","id":1258750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1258673#post1258673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Traditions don't come together. THe shattering happens before the Council of Nine forms. While I can see quite a few groups selling out to be &quot;Faephandus&quot; to serve the fae is to reject ascension. You don't have any form of the Celestial Chorus, You don't have the Order of Hermes, You don't have the Akashic Brotherhood, You don't have the Euthanatos. You Don't have the Ali batini. You potentially have bits that could be the Verbena, the Ecstatics and some of the Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> In the face of the Order of Reason being completely right I'd see the Hermetics Chorus and the Solfacti siding with the Order rather than paradigm warring. The Fae are the threat. Mankind's destiny really is being taken by the monsters(more so than in the standard WOD)<br /> <br /> **<br /> <br /> This is incorrect, the Dark Age Gameline is after the Sundering but before the Shattering. Hermetics Exist. The Messiac precursors of the Choristers Exist, same with most of the others including the Batini and the Euthanatoi. The First Cabal already existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect: The Dark Age Gameline assumes that Hermetics , Messianics and the rest are enemies of each other. There's no Traditions with big T. There's no Council of Nine Mystic Traditions oppsing the forces of the Order of Reason but rather several Fellowships/Paradigms competing against each other<br /> <br /> As per Sorcerers Cruzade, Traditions were founded becuase Sh'zar (The Seer/The Timeless) predicted that the Technocracy would destroy all the ancient mystic traditions (with small t) unless mages all around the world joined together to stop them. The forming of the Traditions as unified group it's a direct consequence of the Order of Reason gaining prominence.<br /> <br /> Since in your timeline that never happened there's no reason for Sh'zar to contact LaSalle and Nightshade and do the great convocation (unless, of course, it's to prevent Fae from taking over the world, but that depends on how heavy handed are the fae going to be against unaligned mages - wich would be most of them because mages are far to proud to bow) - hence there's a bunch of Fellowships that hate each other, and/or a unified front against the Fae that may or may not include most of what we call the Traditions nowdays.<br /> <br /> Also I would want a source for that claim of the First Cabal existing already because I'm pretty sure DA:Mage doesn't mention any native american...and the First Cabal had one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-03-2018, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T13:35:29-07:00","id":1258766,"title":"","content":"Fragile paths talks about the first Cabal, the Proto Dreamspeaker married the Verbena member. They weren\u2019t in Europe so they weren\u2019t in the Dark Age Book.<br /> <br /> I meant that the Individual Traditions, or Fellowships or whatever you call em existed individually. I\u2019m positing here they still would team with the Fae because they see magic dying to science, and their alliance was much more successful. Tradition Mages in general don\u2019t try to rule the world so a system with a greater degree of free trade of ideas and discussion would over all benefit them as they essentially still are free to do their own thing but now benefit from a larger community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T08:08:03-07:00","id":1258876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1258766#post1258766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fragile paths talks about the first Cabal, the Proto Dreamspeaker married the Verbena member. They weren\u2019t in Europe so they weren\u2019t in the Dark Age Book.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they weren't in the Dark Age Book because the events of said book took place before the formation of the First Cabal. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Council_of_Nine_Mystic_Traditions\" target=\"_blank\">The First Cabal was formed in 1466</a> , DA:Mage happens in the 12 century. The Shattering started arround 1347.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I meant that the Individual Traditions, or Fellowships or whatever you call em existed individually. I\u2019m positing here they still would team with the Fae because they see magic dying to science, and their alliance was much more successful. </div> </div> </div>As I already said, the only reason Fellowships joined into Traditions was because Sh'zar saw that only a coalisin of mages would stop the raise of the OoR. There's no way the rise of the OoR can happen in a world ruled by the fae, there's a lot of enemity between Fae and the Technocracy. So, you are saying that faes would have lost to the OoR if Traditions don't form and ally with them?<br /> <br /> That could work. If the Fae can't stop the raise of the Technocracy alone, Sh'zar could have seen the need of mages allying with each other AND the fae.<br /> <br /> However keep in mind that Fellowships were very resistent to this idea of union: LaSalle had to die fighting Masters of his own Fellwoship in order for the OoH to join, Messianic Voices were torn asunder as many wouldn't side with pagans. Euthanatos and Akashicks hate of each other lasted until the modern nights. There needs to be a pressing reason to keep them together after the treath was mostly dealt with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tradition Mages in general don\u2019t try to rule the world so a system with a greater degree of free trade of ideas and discussion would over all benefit them as they essentially still are free to do their own thing but now benefit from a larger community. </div> </div> </div>Well, that's relative. As I see it, mages mostly fall under two groups:<br /> <br /> Most mages don't want to rule, but nearly all factions have an agenda that includes pushing a certain ideology. Most factions of mages have an idea of how the world should look like (be it something established like the city of pymander or merely a world united by faith), and humans serving your Fae overlords usually isn't part of it.<br /> <br /> Other mages are less interested about changing the world and more interested in protecting their comunities. Those could easily accept to be ruled by nice fae, but would try to kill or banish fae that decide to abuse their charges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T16:09:14-07:00","id":1258959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1258673#post1258673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">**<br /> I don't see even if the fae don't rule openly a world where the Fae have taken over supernatural society leading to an earth like the Modern WOD. Especially if they are promoting &quot;More magic&quot;<br /> **<br /> For the same reason they don\u2019t in the normal world. They get in each others way. But perhaps it is a bit better in some ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are saying they don't openly rule areas in DA.. that's wrong? They may not say Rule England but there are huge swaths of territory openly ruled by the fae. Plus this is a world where.. magic should be as ubiquitous as Science is today.. or did the fae basically offer &quot;the Dark ages forever&quot; if so.. you can see why most mages would say &quot;FUCK THIS SHIT&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> **<br /> The Traditions don't come together. THe shattering happens before the Council of Nine forms. While I can see quite a few groups selling out to be &quot;Faephandus&quot; to serve the fae is to reject ascension. You don't have any form of the Celestial Chorus, You don't have the Order of Hermes, You don't have the Akashic Brotherhood, You don't have the Euthanatos. You Don't have the Ali batini. You potentially have bits that could be the Verbena, the Ecstatics and some of the Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> In the face of the Order of Reason being completely right I'd see the Hermetics Chorus and the Solfacti siding with the Order rather than paradigm warring. The Fae are the threat. Mankind's destiny really is being taken by the monsters(more so than in the standard WOD)<br /> **<br /> This is incorrect, the Dark Age Gameline is after the Sundering but before the Shattering. Hermetics Exist. The Messiac precursors of the Choristers Exist, same with most of the others including the Batini and the Euthanatoi. The First Cabal already existed. </div> </div> </div>The Fellowships do not join to form the Traditions. The Fae ruling as Godkings are as much threat to many paradigms as the Order of Reason. If the Fae go on the world dominating offensive this even predates the forming of the Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> Now, if you accept the Tremere &quot;magic is dying&quot; bullshit then there might be an argument.. but their view was likely guided by Saulot since it was all Keikaku as it were for him.<br /> <br /> So rather than say the Messianic Voices having the great shattering into the Cabal of Pure thought and the Celestial Chorus in a world where &quot;Fae want to make people worship false gods&quot; I don't think that split happens. I think the Celestial Chorus keeps with the Cabal of Pure thought.<br /> <br /> Similarly the Craftmasons started as a faction of the Order of Hermes that wanted to reform it, WITH the fae causing issues they are more likely to stay with them than to leave. So you have at least two Traditions probably being the key founders of some sort of &quot;HUmanity fuck yeah!&quot; which would probably take in various Proto Conventions as well.. <br /> <br /> On the other hand some who'd become the Technocracy might have no issue selling out to the Fae.. The High Guild/Syndicate. Selling Fae domination to the world is very much their perview.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I imagine we have a very different set of factions, with different players on the various teams. You don't get either the OOR or The Traditions but &quot;Humanity fuck yeah&quot; &quot;Lets serve the Fae&quot; and &quot;Leave us alone&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> **<br /> If you've been raised to Worship jesus and then suddenly Hades shows up and you've generally been told &quot;Hades was just a mask for demons&quot; all your life are you going to start worshipping him? Because that's going to be the case in Europe. And no the Empire of Stygia is perhaps in one of its more united, and mortals.. ARE a danger to fae at the time so a whole bunch of Ghosts are probably capable at the very least of keeping the Fae from conquering the Dark Kingdoms. The Fae probably have theirown little areas though<br /> <br /> Potentially if all the groups united they could throw off the Fae.. but they won't. They are as much enemies of eachother.<br /> **<br /> Thats not quite accurate. If it was the Fishers or some other religious order would be ruling the Dead, for a time they got close but nope the dead are more pragmatic and often lacking in Faith of unseen angels when Satyrs are right there. But in my canon Angels and Demons exist as Gallain. But huge thing, if you work for Stygia all mass has to come from Plundered Relics and literally making objects out of souls... Fae and Mages can create plasmic matter from their miracle powers. They can literally create Heaven and without literally needing to make the spiked pits or food out of Wraiths. They can literally create the food of paradise from their godlike powers... that absolutely is not something to ignore. And the oldest and most potent of the Dead worship the Old Ways. But either way I view everything from Angels to Egyptian Demons existing among the Fae in some form. </div> </div> </div><br /> The Fishers WERE increadibly powerful. That's why fighting them was such a big thing. Mages have had signficant difficulty in just creating stuff in the shadowlands, and I've never seen anything that says fae can just make stuff there.<br /> <br /> By your same token Giovanni should be complete and utter godkings of the underworld becauase they have the ability to bring things across.<br /> <br /> Now this isn't to say I don't think the Fae won't have territory but rather I don't think they crush the Dark Kingdoms and become the new lords of the Underworld but rather They become competing dark Kingdoms in theirown right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T07:27:35-07:00","id":1259079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the Fae go on the world dominating offensive this even predates the forming of the Order of Reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Convocation of the Ivory Tower happened before the Shattering. If Fae offensive starts a few years after this (given time to adapt to the Changeling Way) the OoR would already have been founded.<br /> <br /> But they may easily decide to fold back into the OoH after the offensive start. OoH was open to dialog back then and obviously dealing with evil mages to protect humanity isn't a priority anymore. It's going to be supper fun: suddenly the small House of the Craftmasons that was rarely seen in the political arena reappears with LOT'S of new allies from every corner of the world and weapons suspiciously similar to those that &quot;the Tremere&quot; used in Mistridge...<br /> <br /> The \u200bHigh Guild may betray them, though, not only because their Paradigm can flourish anyway but also becuse all their founder cares about it's being immortal, and Fae can grant that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-05-2018, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T14:21:16-07:00","id":1259123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259079#post1259079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the Convocation of the Ivory Tower happened before the Shattering. If Fae offensive starts a few years after this (given time to adapt to the Changeling Way) the OoR would already have been founded.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Shattering Ends in 1347, if we go with DA build up its pretty much assumed it begins with the end of the treaty of seasons in 1230 I believe? So if instead of the war of the Seasons they decide to go &quot;LETS RULE HUMANITY&quot; that's what I'm working from a time line that diverges[/QUOTE]<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T21:46:14-07:00","id":1259183,"title":"","content":"It's possible that the Traditions could exist, if Sh'zar's prophecy was different. If, for example, it involved the individual fellowships uniting with each other and the Fae for heretofore unknown levels of knowledge and power. The idea might even have less resistance from some directions, since the benefits would be obvious. <br /> <br /> When did House Diedne get destroyed? Because I was thinking that if you tweaked the timeline a little, they could be useful. An alliance between the Fae and House Diedne would make a lot of sense and could prevent the latter's destruction. An Order of Hermes with an ascendant House Diedne and a weakened House Tremere might look very different from the Order of Hermes in the main setting, which could have an interesting domino effect when it comes to relations with other Fellowships/proto-Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T21:03:49-07:00","id":1259347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259183#post1259183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible that the Traditions could exist, if Sh'zar's prophecy was different. If, for example, it involved the individual fellowships uniting with each other and the Fae for heretofore unknown levels of knowledge and power. The idea might even have less resistance from some directions, since the benefits would be obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>IF power is the only thing that matters the Order of Reason was right there and its always taking recruits. Hell lets talk Tremere if power is all you care about. What makes the Traditions the Traditions was the search for Ascension. the Fae do not offer this. They offer a different form of slavery. Sh'zar's vision is probably not pushing a future where humanity's destiny is stripped from it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When did House Diedne get destroyed? Because I was thinking that if you tweaked the timeline a little, they could be useful. An alliance between the Fae and House Diedne would make a lot of sense and could prevent the latter's destruction. An Order of Hermes with an ascendant House Diedne and a weakened House Tremere might look very different from the Order of Hermes in the main setting, which could have an interesting domino effect when it comes to relations with other Fellowships/proto-Traditions. </div> </div> </div>about 200 or so years before the DA games start?<br /> <br /> I Mean house Marina is already there for the &quot;go help with the fae&quot; but its also.. implied to be heavily corrupted by the Fae, and somewhat distrusted.<br /> <br /> I think you end up with different players in different teams. Some who might become Traditions aren't playing nice with the Fae.. but some who might become the Technocracy might. The Protosyndicate and ProtoVE might make a good jump across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T21:26:07-07:00","id":1259351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259123#post1259123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Shattering Ends in 1347, if we go with DA build up its pretty much assumed it begins with the end of the treaty of seasons in 1230 I believe? So if instead of the war of the Seasons they decide to go &amp;quot;LETS RULE HUMANITY&amp;quot; that's what I'm working from a time line that diverges</div> </div> </div> </div>.<br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> This wasn\u2019t about the Fae taking over the world though. It\u2019s about the Fae taking over/unifying the supernatural side of the world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T21:58:14-07:00","id":1259353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259351#post1259351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.</div> </div> </div> </div>This wasn\u2019t about the Fae taking over the world though. It\u2019s about the Fae taking over/unifying the supernatural side of the world[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I would make a solid argument for various supernaturals behind the scenes ruling the world. Especially the Technocracy, especially in the transition to modernity. If the Fae take the ORder of Reason's place by becoming the top dogs even if they don't rule openly.. they do rule the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T02:20:22-07:00","id":1259371,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s disputable in the Extreme, for one they have other major powers in their way, werewolves, Wan kuei, Camarilla and sabbat, all of whom directly oppose, cept the cammy, techy agendas. And even with this no one changeling would rule as it would be a big mess of Kingdoms, but we would have a tradition of shared territory and exchange of services.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T08:39:02-07:00","id":1259408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259371#post1259371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s disputable in the Extreme, for one they have other major powers in their way, werewolves, Wan kuei, Camarilla and sabbat, all of whom directly oppose, cept the cammy, techy agendas. And even with this no one changeling would rule as it would be a big mess of Kingdoms, but we would have a tradition of shared territory and exchange of services.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And they've been HOW successful in canon timeline? The Technocracy has achieved the vast majority of its Goals. The Weaver is Ascendent. The Camarilla defines Kindred existence and all the other major factions are defined in conflict with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> IF the Fae do not unite to for this timeline change then... it makes little to no sense. So the Salubri go to one fairy-lord for help... that's not an insurmountable challenge for the Tremere. IF they Fae don't unify on some level for this push then someone resisting them easily will. The Order of Reason can and did kill the various disparate magical creatures of europe in canon timeline. IF the fae aren't uniting it changes nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T09:59:34-07:00","id":1259424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259347#post1259347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IF power is the only thing that matters the Order of Reason was right there and its always taking recruits. Hell lets talk Tremere if power is all you care about. What makes the Traditions the Traditions was the search for Ascension. the Fae do not offer this. They offer a different form of slavery. Sh'zar's vision is probably not pushing a future where humanity's destiny is stripped from it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere are exactly what I'm talking about. The Tremere, at this stage of the game, are primarily still mages of the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> The rise of the Order of Reason was not initially about power. The Craftmasons were justly rebelling against the abuses of the Order of Hermes against the common folk. And really, I'd recommend reading the Dark Ages supplement &quot;House Tremere&quot; for some nice insight as to what kind of things the Craftmasons might have been against. The Tremere were likely the worst of the Order of Hermes, but they weren't solely unique.<br /> <br /> Obviously the Order of Reason lost its ideals along the way, culminating in the eventual eradication of the Craftmasons themselves, but if we're talking Dark Ages era, then they're not the group to join if power is ones' sole interest. And it's not like members of the Old Faith or the Spirit Talkers would be remotely welcomed by the Gabrielites or the High Guild.<br /> <br /> The search for Ascension is a relatively new idea. We don't see it in Dark Ages and it's only in its nascent stages in Sorcerer's Crusades. Many mages whose Fellowships will later become Traditions are motivated by the search for power. Heck, many mages in the modern day are more motivated by a lust for power than a true desire for Ascension.<br /> <br /> It would be fairly easy to craft a plausible scenario in which Mistridge and the rise of the Order of Reason still happens, but rather than simply unite for self-protection, Sh'zar has a different vision and instead, the Mages decide to reach out to the Fae for protection from Christopher Wyngarde and his ilk. Or if you would like to keep Sh'zar's motivation pure, then another seer could provide the initial impetus. Perhaps someone the Fae deliberately cultivate for this purpose.<br /> <br /> The Old Faith in particular would already have some ties to the Fae. Some of the holdouts in the Order of Hermes might be attracted to the idea of power and knowledge from the Fae (especially if we tweak the Hermetic history some: keep Diedne around and give Merinita a more prominent role within the Houses, so that there are more pre-existing ties to use.) The other Fellowships might join for the same reason they joined the Traditions in the original setting.<br /> <br /> Obviously, yes, this would be another form of slavery, but it's not like there isn't precedent for that kind of thing. And the Fae might seem a lot more palatable as masters than the creatures that the Infernalists serve.<br /> <br /> I would, of course, agree that there'd be hold outs, but they'd be in a very difficult position, with the wrathful Order of Reason on one side and the Fae-allied not-quite-Traditions on the other. If Ascension still exists as a concept in this particular setting, this would probably be where it develops<br /> <br /> Really, that'd be an interesting element to explore: if we are talking about a world ruled by Fae, then likely there'll also be pockets of resistance in most, if not all, of the supernatural groups (including the Fae themselves, perhaps.) That could be a fun direction to take as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 10-07-2018, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T13:19:38-07:00","id":1259453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would be fairly easy to craft a plausible scenario in which Mistridge and the rise of the Order of Reason still happens, but rather than simply unite for self-protection, Sh'zar has a different vision and instead, the Mages decide to reach out to the Fae for protection from Christopher Wyngarde and his ilk. Or if you would like to keep Sh'zar's motivation pure, then another seer could provide the initial impetus. Perhaps someone the Fae deliberately cultivate for this purpose. </div> </div> </div>The joining of the Fellowships was an epic undertaking that took many lives. And the Traditions join under the premise of it being an egalitarian group - this changes if you demand obedience to the fae overlords. I can't see Choristers and Hermetics not resisting that kind of condition. If the Fae cultivated a seer, it's even harder to see this outcome because it adds the danger of that little factoid being discovered by the mirriad of enemies the idea had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously, yes, this would be another form of slavery, but it's not like there isn't precedent for that kind of thing. And the Fae might seem a lot more palatable as masters than the creatures that the Infernalists serve. </div> </div> </div>That's...not a good precedent...even in the power hungry Order of Hermes serving demons it's seen as the worst kind of sin (while summoning them isn't).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-07-2018, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T13:41:34-07:00","id":1259456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259408#post1259408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And they've been HOW successful in canon timeline? The Technocracy has achieved the vast majority of its Goals. The Weaver is Ascendent. The Camarilla defines Kindred existence and all the other major factions are defined in conflict with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> IF the Fae do not unite to for this timeline change then... it makes little to no sense. So the Salubri go to one fairy-lord for help... that's not an insurmountable challenge for the Tremere. IF they Fae don't unify on some level for this push then someone resisting them easily will. The Order of Reason can and did kill the various disparate magical creatures of europe in canon timeline. IF the fae aren't uniting it changes nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The basic idea is say the traditions were formed here because they saw on the horizon the coming winter and the end of magic if they did nothing. The Fae aren\u2019t ruling mortals like Pope Emperors but instead say are creating Faery Courts as the secret Courts for all supernaturals around the world, with exceptions like the Garou probably keep most of their numbers to themselves but have some members involving the courts. Kind of like if Fae toppled the Kindred hold and just took their territory but opened it up to everyone. So by the present they still have the chimerical shield from Mortal Eyes, but maybe they developed an easier time enchanting supernaturals due to the evolution of magic in this setting. Like maybe in this setting the Dreaming starts tying closer to the Umbra, like the Yin and Yang worlds of the Mirrorlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T13:50:17-07:00","id":1259460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259453#post1259453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The joining of the Fellowships was an epic undertaking that took many lives. And the Traditions join under the premise of it being an egalitarian group - this changes if you demand obedience to the fae overlords. I can't see Choristers and Hermetics not resisting that kind of condition. If the Fae cultivated a seer, it's even harder to see this outcome because it adds the danger of that little factoid being discovered by the mirriad of enemies the idea had.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's...not a good precedent...even in the power hungry Order of Hermes serving demons it's seen as the worst kind of sin (while summoning them isn't).</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m saying they will start out more like Commoners because they are in dire straits. Meaning they nominally are going to be under Noble rule but in reality they will be free to associate with themselves and choose to live in a Court or off the grid that better suits them. Rather then magic being extinguished and everyone losing to an enemy that genocides them. I\u2019m expecting them to have had more civil wars in this setting since there are no returning Kings 500 years later, they are all there from the start.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean you have well over 100k Fae, plus Chimera, enchanted, Kinain, and whatever supernaturals already who swore fealty.<br /> <br /> If the bare minimum you have to do is keep to the old ways, and if a war comes send your share of the defenders yeah it\u2019s not much more irksome then the basic traditions compromise. Especially when now all of a sudden you have access to a large community you don\u2019t have to hide yourself from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T18:15:23-07:00","id":1259495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259424#post1259424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tremere are exactly what I'm talking about. The Tremere, at this stage of the game, are primarily still mages of the Order of Hermes.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the time of the shattering the war had already happened. The order knew about what the Tremere and had fought partial a war with it..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rise of the Order of Reason was not initially about power. The Craftmasons were justly rebelling against the abuses of the Order of Hermes against the common folk. And really, I'd recommend reading the Dark Ages supplement &quot;House Tremere&quot; for some nice insight as to what kind of things the Craftmasons might have been against. The Tremere were likely the worst of the Order of Hermes, but they weren't solely unique. </div> </div> </div>No they weren't. And there were PLENTY of monsters in the Early Order of Reason. And while the Craftmasons weren't all about power... The HIgh Guild and the Cabal of Pure thought were.<br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously the Order of Reason lost its ideals along the way, culminating in the eventual eradication of the Craftmasons themselves, but if we're talking Dark Ages era, then they're not the group to join if power is ones' sole interest. And it's not like members of the Old Faith or the Spirit Talkers would be remotely welcomed by the Gabrielites or the High Guild.[/quote]<br /> <br /> The Order of Reason was all about holding political power. If you don't care about your ideals at all why not join the Cabal of Pure thought or the High guild?<br /> <br /> I never said they would. I said there would be different players in different positions. The Messianic Voices wouldn't have shattered into the Cabal of Pure thought and Celestial Chorus.. in the face of the Order of Reason basically being right.<br /> <br /> The Order of Hermes might lose a few houses but its not going to bend to the Fae anymore than the Order was in canon timeline.. in fact given a choice between Fae overlords and making deals with people who they share paradigmatic ideals with I'd imagine the Order and Craftmasons<br /> <br /> <br /> The Akashics definately wouldn't join either side. Nor might the Euthanatos but many protoecstatic and protoverbenic fellowships might join the fae. The Dreamspeakers are only a tradition by convience of the council so some might fall on either a disparate or fae sides.<br /> <br /> <br /> Equally True I could see the ancestors of the Syndicate and the Void Engineers potentially not joining the Order of reason with the fae offers there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The search for Ascension is a relatively new idea. We don't see it in Dark Ages and it's only in its nascent stages in Sorcerer's Crusades. Many mages whose Fellowships will later become Traditions are motivated by the search for power. Heck, many mages in the modern day are more motivated by a lust for power than a true desire for Ascension. </div> </div> </div>Not really the idea that fellowships aren't the same and fight over stuff is an ancient one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would be fairly easy to craft a plausible scenario in which Mistridge and the rise of the Order of Reason still happens, but rather than simply unite for self-protection, Sh'zar has a different vision and instead, the Mages decide to reach out to the Fae for protection from Christopher Wyngarde and his ilk. Or if you would like to keep Sh'zar's motivation pure, then another seer could provide the initial impetus. Perhaps someone the Fae deliberately cultivate for this purpose. </div> </div> </div>Not really, the Fae start their conquest before Mistridge. The Timeline changes before the Order of Reason or Traditions form. Thus Something else occurs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Old Faith in particular would already have some ties to the Fae. Some of the holdouts in the Order of Hermes might be attracted to the idea of power and knowledge from the Fae (especially if we tweak the Hermetic history some: keep Diedne around and give Merinita a more prominent role within the Houses, so that there are more pre-existing ties to use.) The other Fellowships might join for the same reason they joined the Traditions in the original setting. </div> </div> </div>These are the groups I'd Imagine do align with the Fae. I just don't think you get all 9 of the Council there. Plenty of proto Dreamspeakers aren't going to play nice, some will. Plenty of Old Faith will, some won't. Nothing Messianic is going to play nice. You think the Taftani will play nice? or the Ali Batini?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously, yes, this would be another form of slavery, but it's not like there isn't precedent for that kind of thing. And the Fae might seem a lot more palatable as masters than the creatures that the Infernalists serve. </div> </div> </div>For some, but not for others. I don't imagine the Order of Hermes being any more prone to serving the Fae as serving Demons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would, of course, agree that there'd be hold outs, but they'd be in a very difficult position, with the wrathful Order of Reason on one side and the Fae-allied not-quite-Traditions on the other. If Ascension still exists as a concept in this particular setting, this would probably be where it develops<br /> <br /> Really, that'd be an interesting element to explore: if we are talking about a world ruled by Fae, then likely there'll also be pockets of resistance in most, if not all, of the supernatural groups (including the Fae themselves, perhaps.) That could be a fun direction to take as well. </div> </div> </div><br /> Ascension has always been a drive of mages, plenty try to ignore it but the concept of &quot;I am not a slave to monsters from beyond reality&quot; is pretty common. Something I'd imagine the Craftmasons and much of the Order of hermes agreeing on especially as the Craftmasons don't break away before the &quot;Serve or die&quot; happens.<br /> <br /> So the Order of Humanity<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes<br /> Messianic Voices<br /> Artificers<br /> Solfacti<br /> Krisfai<br /> Batini?<br /> Wu Lung?<br /> Ngoma?<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Traditions&quot;<br /> <br /> Old Faith<br /> Some spirit talkers<br /> Some Ecstatics<br /> High Guild<br /> Celestial masters<br /> Void Seekers.<br /> <br /> Disparates:<br /> Euthanatos<br /> Akashic brotherhood<br /> Taftani<br /> Many other dreamspeakers<br /> Many other Ecstatic cultural traditions<br /> Sisters<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259456#post1259456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The basic idea is say the traditions were formed here because they saw on the horizon the coming winter and the end of magic if they did nothing. The Fae aren\u2019t ruling mortals like Pope Emperors but instead say are creating Faery Courts as the secret Courts for all supernaturals around the world, with exceptions like the Garou probably keep most of their numbers to themselves but have some members involving the courts. Kind of like if Fae toppled the Kindred hold and just took their territory but opened it up to everyone. So by the present they still have the chimerical shield from Mortal Eyes, but maybe they developed an easier time enchanting supernaturals due to the evolution of magic in this setting. Like maybe in this setting the Dreaming starts tying closer to the Umbra, like the Yin and Yang worlds of the Mirrorlands.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then.. they get their asses handed to them by anyone who can organize a large group. SO the Tremere destroy the Salubri and their few fae. The ORder of Reason just wins.. etc. Either the Fae organize or they lose. That's just how things work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T18:15:49-07:00","id":1259496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259453#post1259453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The joining of the Fellowships was an epic undertaking that took many lives. And the Traditions join under the premise of it being an egalitarian group - this changes if you demand obedience to the fae overlords. I can't see Choristers and Hermetics not resisting that kind of condition. If the Fae cultivated a seer, it's even harder to see this outcome because it adds the danger of that little factoid being discovered by the mirriad of enemies the idea had.<br /> <br /> That's...not a good precedent...even in the power hungry Order of Hermes serving demons it's seen as the worst kind of sin (while summoning them isn't).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by the idea that it's not a good precedent. We have definitely seen examples in the core setting of Hermetics becoming Infernalists, and eventually finding themselves serving demons. We can look at the kind of individual circumstances that led to those, admittedly very rare, falls in canon and figure out ways to make those circumstances more universal (with a Fae theme instead of a demonic one). Obviously the power hungry Order of Hermes wouldn't and didn't decide as a majority to serve demons in the canon setting, but we're not talking about the canon setting.<br /> <br /> We're talking about a potential alternate universe/timeline and obviously things will have to be changed to make it work. The Fae need to be more aggressive and proactive. The Mages have to be desperate or ambitious enough to make deals that they didn't in canon. The interesting part of this kind of thought experiment is thinking of what needs to be changed for this to happen.<br /> <br /> For example, the Choristers would doubtless be resistant to Fae in their natural forms. But might the Fae be able to masquerade themselves as angels, saints or other Celestial beings? Heck, depending on what you decide is the base cosmology of the universe, the Fae might well be angels. Or at least similarly creatures of dream and belief.<br /> <br /> The Hermetics would need a more subtle approach: one that looks more like a bargain than mastery at first. The Fae might play at serving Mages, even, until the Mages eventually realize that they're the ones being manipulated. It would take a very long time, but the Fae, in this scenario, would have time. <br /> <br /> The proto-Akashic and proto-Euthanatos... Okay, I admit, I have no idea where to even start with them. They might need to not exist in this setting, or to be so changed as to be unrecognizable. Or maybe the Fae just gets rid of them, presuming, of course, that they have the power to do that. (That's also the likely solution for the inevitably intractable members of any of the Fellowships/proto-Traditions)<br /> <br /> I'd imagine anyone who seriously wants to use this idea in a game would spend a lot more time than I did figuring out how to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 10-07-2018, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T18:31:15-07:00","id":1259500,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting though to see what the modern world of darkness would look like under Fae domination, though. Assuming it's remotely recognizable as our world. (Would the Fae allow the Industrial Revolution to happen, for example? What would need to happen for them to allow it?)<br /> <br /> I think by this time we wouldn't see any of the recognizable Traditions or Fellowships. The original groups would likely have ended up dissolved either directly because of the Fae, or because Mage society would be so transformed by their relationship with the Fae as to be unrecognizable. I suspect the Fae would want to keep Mages fairly separate from each other, since allowing a bunch of mages to gather and share ideas/ambition seems like a really bad idea to me. We know what Mages can do once they gather in groups.<br /> <br /> Would the Camarilla and Sabbat still exist? Would the Camarilla look more like a faery House/Court than it does in the modern setting? Would the Sabbat utilize a lot of Unseelie practices? I feel like the Werewolves might be able to work something out with the Fae, but I admit, I've never really had a good grasp on that gameline.<br /> <br /> I can't really imagine how the more modern splats like the Hunters, Revised Mummies or Demons could work in this scenario, though. Maybe the Demons are just lost/abandoned/confused Fae? You could maybe spin some kind of comparison between the Demons' relationship to Faith and Dreams/Mists?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 10-07-2018, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T22:47:03-07:00","id":1259534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259496#post1259496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what you mean by the idea that it's not a good precedent. We have definitely seen examples in the core setting of Hermetics becoming Infernalists, and eventually finding themselves serving demons. We can look at the kind of individual circumstances that led to those, admittedly very rare, falls in canon and figure out ways to make those circumstances more universal (with a Fae theme instead of a demonic one). Obviously the power hungry Order of Hermes wouldn't and didn't decide as a majority to serve demons in the canon setting, but we're not talking about the canon setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean it's that Infernalists are hated by most factions of mages, and whatever the reason individual factions have to hate them, the fact that they 're hated alone proves that Demons failed to make the main factions into Infernalist cults - and not because they lack power to appear as angels or whatever they want.<br /> <br /> Demons failed to enslave all mages before, showing as an example of mages in general (as opposed to individual cases) choosing to eschew power in the name of being their own masters (which happens to be a big deal among the OoH). Even more it shows examples of factions of mages being destroyed by their peers because they choose to follow demons<br /> <br /> One could argue that Fae-friends could/should follow a similar route if they don't do something radically different than Demons. Not trying to enslave mages or humanity to their capricious whims it's a good start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, the Choristers would doubtless be resistant to Fae in their natural forms. But might the Fae be able to masquerade themselves as angels, saints or other Celestial beings? Heck, depending on what you decide is the base cosmology of the universe, the Fae might well be angels. Or at least similarly creatures of dream and belief.<br /> <br /> The Hermetics would need a more subtle approach: one that looks more like a bargain than mastery at first. The Fae might play at serving Mages, even, until the Mages eventually realize that they're the ones being manipulated. It would take a very long time, but the Fae, in this scenario, would have time.<br /> <br /> The proto-Akashic and proto-Euthanatos... Okay, I admit, I have no idea where to even start with them. They might need to not exist in this setting, or to be so changed as to be unrecognizable. Or maybe the Fae just gets rid of them, presuming, of course, that they have the power to do that. (That's also the likely solution for the inevitably intractable members of any of the Fellowships/proto-Traditions)<br /> <br /> I'd imagine anyone who seriously wants to use this idea in a game would spend a lot more time than I did figuring out how to do it. </div> </div> </div>Soo...in your version faes manage to fool every existant faction of mages (which, unsurprisingly, makes mages look like fools), maybe erase some. One wonders how it's that the OoR is still a treath if Fae are that capable (what?, they can't transform into muses? - how ironic). O yeah...it's because you need the OoR for the mages to join into the Traditions in the first place. Surely that was part of the Fae plot too, it wouldn't surprise me in the slightest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-08-2018, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T23:34:31-07:00","id":1259540,"title":"","content":"Again there seems to be a miscommunication. I\u2019m saying the Fae conquer because they have way more in terms of number then their enemies. They conquer en mass and then war against each other later after they break the back of their rivals.<br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t about a timeline where the traditions team up with the techies, it\u2019s one where the Fae exercise their greater then ten times number of Mages and shatter them.<br /> <br /> Their version of the traditions probably aren\u2019t the same either. Like the dreamspeakers would have a connection with he Nunnehi and others, the Wu Lung the Hsien, ect. Likely they could even back a sub group from the Hermetics/Verbena/Oldways/Valdermen into a full blown new tradition of Fae Mages.<br /> <br /> How are the Tremere going to gather bigger numbers? I\u2019m saying in this setting there are over 100k Changelings alone, not to mention Inanimae and other Gallain. How many Tremere do you think exist back in the day when they were new, war weary and confined mostly to Europe and the Holy land.<br /> <br /> <br /> The premise is already there is a Different Traditions in this timeline and they are dominant with Fae Aid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T11:14:51-07:00","id":1259623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259534#post1259534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Soo...in your version faes manage to fool every existant faction of mages (which, unsurprisingly, makes mages look like fools), maybe erase some. One wonders how it's that the OoR is still a treath if Fae are that capable (what?, they can't transform into muses? - how ironic). O yeah...it's because you need the OoR for the mages to join into the Traditions in the first place. Surely that was part of the Fae plot too, it wouldn't surprise me in the slightest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you actually read the first post in this thread? Per the scenario established by the OP, the Order of Reason ISN'T a threat. It's &quot;already&quot; (presumably in the present day of the scenario) been broken by the Fae. The mages who are or would be the Traditions have a new role entirely working as wisemen and advisors to the Fae.<br /> <br /> I was talking about ways that this could possibly come about. Does this mean a lot of Mages look like fools? Probably. But it's not like we don't have canon setting examples of mages making both understandable and really bizarre mistakes. Some, I'm sure, would have a better understanding of what's actually going on and would join the Fae willingly. Some likely would rebel entirely, but in this scenario, the Fae are powerful enough that those rebellious mages would have to be hiding very well or wiped out entirely.<br /> <br /> I tend to prefer the former, because it allows for fun within the game. And also, as a Mage player primarily, if I were running this scenario, it'd be as a Mage game, with the rebellious/independent mages as the underdog protagonists. It'd be interesting to explore Mage's themes in a supernatural society that's already primarily mystical, but still, in many ways, as constrained and oppressive as the main setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T11:59:43-07:00","id":1259633,"title":"","content":"Exactly as Kalimana said.<br /> <br /> I was trying to think of a group that could pull this off, Vampires don\u2019t have mystical puissance, and could only get the numbers temporarily before it would fall apart. I mean I suppose they could pull it off in a setting where he antes awaken and make a buttload more 4th gen. Wraiths have the numbers but also less personal power. Fera are very potent, but they already are burning the candle both ends to keep the world from ending and they are going extinct. Fallen are the only other ones with numbers and individual power to pull it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T17:01:47-07:00","id":1259683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259623#post1259623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you actually read the first post in this thread? Per the scenario established by the OP, the Order of Reason ISN'T a threat. It's &quot;already&quot; (presumably in the present day of the scenario) been broken by the Fae. The mages who are or would be the Traditions have a new role entirely working as wisemen and advisors to the Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then there's not Traditions at all...for the reasons mentioned in this thread that were never refuted and were, in fact, accepted by both of you:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The other Fellowships might join for the same reason they joined the Traditions in the original setting</b>. </div> </div> </div>That is the danger presented by the OoR...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I\u2019m saying they will start out more like Commoners because they are in dire straits.</b> Meaning they nominally are going to be under Noble rule but in reality they will be free to associate with themselves and choose to live in a Court or off the grid that better suits them.<b> Rather then magic being extinguished and everyone losing to an enemy that genocides them</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalinara</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>It would be fairly easy to craft a plausible scenario in which Mistridge and the rise of the Order of Reason still happens</b>, but rather than simply unite for self-protection, Sh'zar has a different vision and instead, the <b>Mages decide to reach out to the Fae for protection from Christopher Wyngarde and his ilk.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Both you and Eldagusto are saying that Mages joined because this enemy that wants to genocide them is such a big deal that serving the fae it's now a good idea - that makes OoR more dangerous than in the cannon setting because in the canon it wasn't such a threat in the begining, to the point that many members of the OoH were happier dealing with them than with the other Traditions . All of which seem to point that, as I said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">. O yeah...it's because you need the OoR for the mages to join into the Traditions in the first place. Surely that was part of the Fae plot too, it wouldn't surprise me in the slightest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously Fae planed everything. they were the cause of the temporary rise of power of the OoR so mages join them, and latter they destroyed the Order of Reason. [Irony]And they surelly did all of this this while raping Sh'zar, because why not? [/Irony].<br /> <br /> It was supposed to be ironical, to satirize the amount of plot armor you were summoning - because you made the faes so much more capable than mages that they end seeming like the authors pet. But I forgot the tags.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259623#post1259623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking about ways that this could possibly come about. Does this mean a lot of Mages look like fools? Probably. But it's not like we don't have canon setting examples of mages making both understandable and really bizarre mistakes. Some, I'm sure, would have a better understanding of what's actually going on and would join the Fae willingly. Some likely would rebel entirely, but in this scenario, the Fae are powerful enough that those rebellious mages would have to be hiding very well or wiped out entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere rising just needs a few clans and one Tradition to be fooled, and the Tremere raising has been very criticized, hasn't it? These kind of plots that require every actor but the ST pets to be fooled and act out of character have been vilified in RPG comunity before. I just don't think they should be an example to follow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to think of a group that could pull this off, Vampires don\u2019t have mystical puissance, and could only get the numbers temporarily before it would fall apart. I mean I suppose they could pull it off in a setting where he antes awaken and make a buttload more 4th gen. Wraiths have the numbers but also less personal power. Fera are very potent, but they already are burning the candle both ends to keep the world from ending and they are going extinct. Fallen are the only other ones with numbers and individual power to pull it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pulling that off has nothing to do with numbers, it has to do with how the different groups formed in the first place, and how a slavering force brought uppone them would change their outlook. <b>All the critic it's about trying to avoid steamrolling the themes of the other factions</b>. It's hard to imagine most mages being content as &quot;Commoner&quot;, it's WAY harder to believe most mages will chose to become slaves as per the &quot;exactly as Kalinara said&quot; scenario.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you have Lian's scenario (team fae vs team human, with most factions of mages being team human). That's an example of trying not to not steamroll the themes of mage factions in a world were Faes did such a hostile takeover. Those factions that were sympathetic to the fae or have no problem with being second class citizens join the Fae, the rest of the factions, the ones who care about humanity, freedom, or are too proud to bend their knees to the fae overlords band against them. No one needs to be a fool nor act out of character. Faes can be the overdogs and an overaching force that has to be aknowledged by every splat without being mary sues protected by fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-08-2018, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T17:34:28-07:00","id":1259688,"title":"","content":"You do realize that this is Eldagusto's thread about Eldagusto's specific idea, right?<br /> <br /> No one's saying you have to play in this hypothetical scenario, if the idea that the fae being &quot;mary sues protected by fiat&quot; bothers you. For one thing, I didn't get the impression that that's the point at all. Simply, to get to the present day scenario that Eldagusto's proposing, a lot of changes need to happen to canon. I've proposed some ideas in that direction that may or may not work for you, perhaps you have some ideas as well?<br /> <br /> Lian's ideas are also interesting, but it sounds like they may not be entirely compatible with Eldagusto's original concept. (Or perhaps they are? I won't try to speak to Eldagusto.) But I feel like maybe the idea of whether Lian's concept is preferable to Eldagusto's concept might be better explored in a more general alternate setting themed thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 10-08-2018, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T18:03:16-07:00","id":1259694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259688#post1259688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize that this is Eldagusto's thread about Eldagusto's specific idea, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and that's exactly what I'm analizing. This forum allows to criticize ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No one's saying you have to play in this hypothetical scenario, if the idea that the fae being &quot;mary sues protected by fiat&quot; bothers you. For one thing, I didn't get the impression that that's the point at all. Simply, to get to the present day scenario that Eldagusto's proposing, a lot of changes need to happen to canon. </div> </div> </div>And I can't say I don't like your idea, and explain why?. I don't think my reasonings were wrong, trough I see now that my irony was uncalled for. I should have explained why I think such plots are a worse idea than the original idea Eldagusto had rather than thinking it was obvious .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lian's ideas are also interesting, but it sounds like they may not be entirely compatible with Eldagusto's original concept. (Or perhaps they are? I won't try to speak to Eldagusto.) But I feel like maybe the idea of whether Lian's concept is preferable to Eldagusto's concept might be better explored in a more general alternate setting themed thread. </div> </div> </div>Lian's concept was a direct critic and a challenge to Eldagusto's assumptions, there's no better thread to say that I think that those are right.<br /> <br /> Also, the idea of Traditions happily joining with the Fae against the OoR, that was the original assumption, and the assumption I and Lian criticized, seems to have been abandoned. And I wasn't able to adjust in time<br /> <br /> We went from this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant that the Individual Traditions, or Fellowships or whatever you call em existed individually. I\u2019m positing here they still would team with the Fae because they see magic dying to science, and their alliance was much more successful.</div> </div> </div> </div>To this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn\u2019t about a timeline where the traditions team up with the techies, it\u2019s one where the Fae exercise their greater then ten times number of Mages and shatter them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite a change in the discourse, don't you think?<br /> <br /> Now all my critics are invalid, because the frame did change quite a lot and if mages are forced into slavery then what they believe or what would/should have done doesn't really matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-08-2018, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T18:52:21-07:00","id":1259699,"title":"","content":"Organization is more important than numbers. People go on and on about how much bullshit the Tremere pulled but... its pretty solidly written out in the DA book. The Tremere win because they are scarily organized. Yes if the Tzim could throw their full might at the Tremere they would have won.. except every Tzim can't throw their full might at anything because Every Vovoid is a god of hisown domain and will bow to no man. The same thing with House Tytalus who.. were the only members of the order of Hermes who took the Tremere thing more seriously than &quot;NOW WE CAN KICK THEM OUT&quot; IF you can get more than 3 Gangrel to work together.. congradulations you've formed the Camarilla.. and so on.<br /> <br /> For the Fae to take the Cam or the Order of Reason's position in an alternative timeline requires a level of organization that lets them properly use their massive numbers. You have to unite the Courts and not let there be random fae courts who don't really get along because we know other groups can unite. So.. they take over a few places.. someone forms the Order of Reason and bam they win. The Fae can't offer the Salubri protection if no two fae overlords agree on how and why.. etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for whether we should talk about ideas posted on these threads. Either we discuss what we think is a plausible timeline.. or we don't discuss things. People can craft from it the game setting they want or not. I am not going to break into your homes and make you use my ideas. IF you don't want to use them.. don't. If you don't want your ideas picked appart and commented on.. blog posts exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T19:13:10-07:00","id":1259706,"title":"","content":"True, Fae would have to be organized.<br /> <br /> I imagine that's quite possible - the fae not only have a clear hierarchy (Noble-Commoner) but also have supernatural means of enforcing it, including Oaths that are both magical and socially compelling. They have all the *mechanics* to have a very tight organization if a sufficently puissant leader were to appear and unite the horde. All they need it's one heck of a King<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T19:34:24-07:00","id":1259712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259706#post1259706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, Fae would have to be organized.<br /> <br /> I imagine that's quite possible - the fae not only have a clear hierarchy (Noble-Commoner) but also have supernatural means of enforcing it, including Oaths that are both magical and socially compelling. They have all the *mechanics* to have a very tight organization if a sufficently puissant leader were to appear and unite the horde. All they need it's one heck of a King<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They wouldn't even need to use numbers really We might even have a minority of Fae a part of it but since they are the ROME they can impose things far beyond their borders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T21:08:51-07:00","id":1259729,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not a change in discourse, it\u2019s clarification. And they aren\u2019t teaming up to fight the Order of Reason, they are teaming up because they see that magic is dying and the Fae are right and Winter is coming. It\u2019s align with the rest of the supernatural world or be kicked to the periphery and trampled.<br /> <br /> It sounds like you want to discuss a different alternate timeline the premise of this thread?<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m positing that certain things are going to parallel even with different actors in place. It\u2019s like when you go to different Marvel Universes in the Multiverse with the Illuminati or the Exiles and you see in one world Magneto and Doom are member but Xavier isn\u2019t, or Mimic Joined the X-men early on so Cyclops never developed leadership, or the Skrulls take over Earth in the 1800s but you still have a boom of Marvels 100 years later even though history is vastly different Reed still has stretch powers because instead of piloting his own ship he pilots a skrull vessel and Hulk exists because a gamma meltdown occurs in a human slave colony.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m pointing out things that I am proposing have happened for this thought exercise. You both really don\u2019t like the basic premise, that is fine but I don\u2019t see why we still can\u2019t discuss it? I mean you could also start a spin off thread discussing your proposed idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry I\u2019ve had to use my phone to interact with the forums lately since my puter is trashed, so it\u2019s hard for me to quote and such.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I\u2019ve already pointed out it\u2019s intentional the Mages are going to chafe under this system of rule. That is literally part of the whole idea, a source of conflict but still a method to hav multiple supernaturals interact. It may even be kind of like the matrix where Mages hidden off the grid (maybe horizon realms represent Mages who want to take back Earth) jack in still to talk and deal with kosher court members.<br /> <br /> As I\u2019ve pointed out even in the default setting commoners don\u2019t even like the system of nobility<br /> <br /> <br /> And it does make a difference with numbers, say there are less then 10k Mages but their are about 200kish Fae along with 50-100k miscellaneous aligned major splat supernaturals and even more minor splats. If you are a dreamspeaker Inuit shaman why wouldn\u2019t you align with an Inua spirit, or a Medicine man down south why wouldn\u2019t you work with a Kachina over a colonialist hermetic? Why wouldn\u2019t a Houngan work with an Eshu over an atheist Adept? Why wouldn\u2019t a Valderman work with an Alfar to fight against the sciencers and their Christgod?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T21:10:09-07:00","id":1259731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1259712#post1259712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They wouldn't even need to use numbers really We might even have a minority of Fae a part of it but since they are the ROME they can impose things far beyond their borders.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Fae are everywhere so I\u2019m saying they will already be in the cities with the humans, and a good amount of them will also be in the Wilderness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T21:22:57-07:00","id":1259733,"title":"","content":"And it was other people\u2019s ideas that the techies and traditions team up against the Fae, that was never the basic premise here. The basic premise many supernaturals chose to join this society, those who didn\u2019t were driven out or nearly eradicated as the Fae consolidated territory and places of power. So the strongest most numerous Mages would be with the Fae, or at least Neutral, those purely against them would be more ragtag by the present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T12:39:21-07:00","id":1259859,"title":"","content":"I think you heavily over estimate Fae numbers. But say there are 10x as many Fae as Mages. But Fae spread out so there's one in alot of places but mages are pressured by this to Clump.(The same is True with Kindred. They are also pressured to focus on smaller areas). This means that if the fae aren't organized then... if you get like 1/3 of the mages to organize then.. they can throw greater numbers at a smaller area because the Fae can't properly make use of their numbers. <br /> <br /> This is both what the Order of Reason did and the Tremere did. They organized. Other numerically superior Groups failed. Hell we can look at Real life where this proved true(early rome, British empire etc)<br /> <br /> And no, my premise is not &quot;Traditions join wit the Technocracy to fight fae&quot; but rather The fellowships shake out differently. A signficant faction join with the fae in my view... I just don't think you get the same teams. I gave them over half the Order of Reason. Its.. also debatable where the Cosians would fall. THough they and the solfacti could unite into a single fellowship.. <br /> <br /> I see the Majority of the Order of Hermes not bending. But there are people who will but say you trade house Meritina for the Returning Craftmasons.<br /> <br /> The Messianic Voices don't break.<br /> <br /> The Coisians and Solfacti make a single alchemy/healing group.<br /> <br /> The Wu Lung also not being of the &quot;bowing to shen&quot; attitude.. and quite possibly backed up by Hsien who.. are not going to be instituting Western Fae practices might be the most solid magical leader.<br /> <br /> The Artificers... who basically will get driven to the edges of the world by the fae anyway sure Nockers exist.. but these are the men of iron. <br /> <br /> Krisfari-don't see why they'd go anywhere else really.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Ngoma(this really depends)<br /> <br /> Maybe the Batini(also depends...)<br /> <br /> So you have a mimimum of six fellowships and a maximum of 9.<br /> <br /> Fae siders.<br /> <br /> Verbena<br /> Some Ecstatics(the issue here is organizing ecstatic traditions is hard)<br /> Some Dreamspeakers(same issue)<br /> Valdermen<br /> High Guild<br /> Celestial Masters<br /> Void Seekers.<br /> House Meritina<br /> <br /> that's 8 minimum.. but you could easily break up the fellowships forced together under the banner of the Seers of Chronos and Dreamspeakers into multiple groups. Honestly I'd imagine more Ecstatic traditions fall towards the Fae than away and generally more so than pure shamanic ones. So you could easily hit 13 factions.<br /> <br /> The Ngoma are iffy in who they join. While they are very much &quot;humanity fuck yeah....&quot; Do the African fae really play the same games as European? If they have a different situation <br /> <br /> The Batini are natural bridge builders they could easily play neutral party keeping bothsides from exploding.<br /> <br /> <br /> With the rest hitting the Crafts/Disparate level.<br /> <br /> <br /> But as I've continually said the BIG faction is the fae support faction. The other side is still though a potential threat like not a beaten animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T15:33:31-07:00","id":1259881,"title":"","content":"Then it sounds like we are more or less in Accordence. Might change the Hsien some but I will treat them like they are emperors of their territory but they have relations with the other Fae. In this setting the other continents might keep their ruler but I\u2019m thinking since the Nunnehi teamed up with the Inanimae and the pure tribes America may have a split rule with native powers keeping places of power. The wyld west with the Garou would also be different maybe the Croatan still live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T16:45:02-07:00","id":1259894,"title":"","content":"Also pointing out the Changeling numbers are huge by default. They have Courts bigger then Vampires, without the blood population restrictions, and their hierarchy is built off it, they have lots of positions. The manikins alone are suspected to have more the 7k in Europe alone. Changelings were the only modern group to regularly raise small armies for things like civil war. And Dark Age had literal standing armies in Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T20:30:02-08:00","id":1288826,"title":"","content":"Have you read the Mercy Thompson novels by Patricia Briggs? Her version of arcadia is a sentient self aware being who kicked the gentry out. The fae are the biggest and most powerful group around. Strong enough to make the US government mind it's manners most of the time. The werewolves have recently come out. The vampires are still hidden. The mages are mostly hidden. I recommend the series, check your local library and see what you think of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T21:19:08-08:00","id":1288837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1258338-what-if-the-fae-rules-a-unified-supernatural-society?p=1288826#post1288826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read the Mercy Thompson novels by Patricia Briggs? Her version of arcadia is a sentient self aware being who kicked the gentry out. The fae are the biggest and most powerful group around. Strong enough to make the US government mind it's manners most of the time. The werewolves have recently come out. The vampires are still hidden. The mages are mostly hidden. I recommend the series, check your local library and see what you think of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never heard of this, I\u2019ll look it up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}